1. Purpose
This policy defines the reimbursement rules and spending limits for {{ expense_type }} expenses
incurred by HYTech Solutions employees on approved business activities.
All claims must be submitted within {{ submission_deadline_days }} calendar days of the expense date.

2. Scope
This policy applies to all HYTech Solutions employees and contractors who incur {{ expense_type }}
expenses in the course of authorised business travel or remote work activities.
Expenses claimed in currencies other than {{ currency }} will be converted at the corporate rate
on the date of expenditure.

3. Spending Limits
The following table specifies the maximum reimbursable amounts per {{ expense_type }} event
by employee role and region. Amounts are in {{ currency }}.

| Expense Type | Role | Region | Limit ({{ currency }}) | Approval Required |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
{% for row in spending_limit_rows %}
| {{ row.expense_type }} | {{ row.role }} | {{ row.region }} | {{ row.limit }} | {{ row.approval_required }} |
{% endfor %}

4. Receipt Requirements
Receipts are mandatory for all expenses exceeding {{ receipt_required_threshold }} {{ currency }}.
Itemised receipts must be uploaded via the Expense Management Portal within {{ receipt_upload_days }} days.
Missing receipts for amounts above the threshold will result in claim rejection.
{% if digital_receipt_accepted %}
Digital receipts (PDF, email confirmation) are accepted in lieu of physical receipts.
{% endif %}

5. Approval Process
{% if approval_required %}
All {{ expense_type }} expenses require pre-approval from the direct manager before commitment.
Claims above {{ senior_approval_threshold }} {{ currency }} require secondary approval from the Finance Lead.
Pre-approval requests must be submitted at least {{ pre_approval_lead_days }} business days before travel.
{% else %}
{{ expense_type }} expenses below the spending limit do not require pre-approval.
Expenses above the spending limit require manager approval before reimbursement is processed.
{% endif %}

6. Exceptions
Expenses that exceed the stated limits may be approved in exceptional circumstances:
- Client entertainment events with documented business justification
- Emergency travel or accommodation required due to safety concerns
- Events in high-cost locations where standard limits are insufficient (requires Finance Lead sign-off)
Exceptions must be approved in writing before the expense is incurred where reasonably practicable.

7. Reimbursement Timeline
Approved claims are reimbursed within {{ reimbursement_timeline_days }} calendar days of approval.
Claims submitted after the {{ submission_deadline_days }}-day window may be rejected at the discretion
of the Finance Lead. Queries regarding pending claims should be directed to {{ finance_owner }}.

8. Non-Reimbursable Expenses
The following {{ expense_type }} expenses are not reimbursable under any circumstances:
{% for item in non_reimbursable %}
- {{ item }}
{% endfor %}

9. Policy Compliance and Audit
The Finance Operations team conducts quarterly audits of {{ expense_type }} expense claims.
Policy violations may result in repayment obligations and disciplinary action.
All records are retained for {{ audit_retention_years }} years in compliance with statutory requirements.

